7,"t":"gain","x":"1327: Kampili falls.","cp":"kampili-kingdom","cpn":"Kampili Kingdom","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kampili_Kingdom","c":3},{"y":1327,"t":"capital_move","x":"1327: the capital moves to Daulatabad.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muhammad_bin_Tughluq","c":3},{"y":1330,"t":"gain","x":"1330: Munger is annexed.","cp":"Bengal (local rulers; the page names none)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muhammad_bin_Tughluq","c":3},{"y":1335,"t":"loss","x":"1335: Ma'bar secedes.","cp":"madurai-sultanate","cpn":"Madurai Sultanate","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Delhi_Sultanate","c":3},{"y":1335,"t":"capital_move","x":"1335: the capital returns to Delhi.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muhammad_bin_Tughluq","c":3},{"y":1336,"t":"loss","x":"1336: Warangal is lost.","cp":"musunuri-nayaks","cpn":"Musunuri Nayaks","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tughlaq_dynasty","c":3},{"y":1336,"t":"loss","x":"1336: Vijayanagara rises on Kampili's land.","cp":"vijayanagara-empire","cpn":"Vijayanagara Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kampili_Kingdom","c":2},{"y":1336,"t":"contest_end","x":"1336: Singoli ends the fight for Mewar.","cp":"kingdom-of-mewar","cpn":"Kingdom of Mewar","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muhammad_bin_Tughluq","c":2},{"y":1336,"t":"loss","x":"1336: Mewar is lost and the contest that opened in 1326 ends.","cp":"kingdom-of-mewar","cpn":"Kingdom of Mewar","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muhammad_bin_Tughluq","c":2},{"y":1339,"t":"loss","x":"1339: the east is gone.","cp":"sultanate-of-bengal","cpn":"Bengal Sultanate","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tughlaq_dynasty","c":2},{"y":1347,"t":"loss","x":"1347: the Deccan secedes.","cp":"bahmani-sultanate","cpn":"Bahmani Sultanate","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muhammad_bin_Tughluq","c":3},{"y":1351,"t":"loss","x":"1351: Sind secedes.","m":3,"cp":"sind-samma-dynasty","cpn":"Samma dynasty","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samma_dynasty","c":3},{"y":1352,"t":"loss","x":"1352: Cliopatria's shape drops the plains south and east of the Delhi core.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Firuz_Shah_Tughlaq","c":1},{"y":1360,"t":"vassal_start","x":"1360: Jajnagar pays tribute.","cp":"eastern-ganga-kingdom","cpn":"Eastern Ganga Kingdom","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Firuz_Shah_Tughlaq","c":3},{"y":1363,"t":"vassal_start","x":"1363: Thatta submits.","cp":"sind-samma-dynasty","cpn":"Samma dynasty","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Firuz_Shah_Tughlaq","c":3},{"y":1388,"t":"vassal_end","x":"1388: Firuz dies (20 September 1388) and the Jajnagar tribute is closed with his reign; the page records one levy and no continuing obligation.","cp":"eastern-ganga-kingdom","cpn":"Eastern Ganga Kingdom","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Firuz_Shah_Tughlaq","c":1},{"y":1388,"t":"vassal_end","x":"1388: Firuz dies and the Thatta tribute is closed with his reign; the Samma page has the Sammas 'subject to Delhi for a time' without an end, and Cliopatria draws Sind as the Sammas' alone.","cp":"sind-samma-dynasty","cpn":"Samma dynasty","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Firuz_Shah_Tughlaq","c":1},{"y":1394,"t":"loss","x":"1394: Jaunpur is founded under Malik Sarwar.","cp":"jaunpur-sultanate","cpn":"Jaunpur Sultanate","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaunpur_Sultanate","c":2},{"y":1394,"t":"loss","x":"1394: Gujarat declares independence.","cp":"gujarat-sultanate","cpn":"Gujarat Sultanate","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gujarat_Sultanate","c":3},{"y":1394,"t":"contest_start","x":"1394: two sultans.","cp":"Nusrat Shah (Firozabad)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nasir-ud-Din_Mahmud_Shah_Tughluq","c":2},{"y":1397,"t":"contest_end","x":"1397: the split ends.","cp":"Nusrat Shah (Firozabad)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Delhi_Sultanate","c":2},{"y":1398,"t":"occupation_start","x":"December 1398: Timur sacks Delhi.","m":12,"cp":"timurid-empire","cpn":"Timurid Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Delhi_(1398)","c":3},{"y":1399,"t":"occupation_end","x":"1399: Timur leaves.","cp":"timurid-empire","cpn":"Timurid Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Delhi_Sultanate","c":2},{"y":1401,"t":"loss","x":"1401: Malwa becomes an independent realm.","cp":"malwa-sultanate","cpn":"Malwa Sultanate","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Malwa_Sultanate","c":2},{"y":1402,"t":"loss","x":"1402: the Punjab passes to Timur's governor.","cp":"timurid-empire","cpn":"Timurid Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nasir-ud-Din_Mahmud_Shah_Tughluq","c":1},{"y":1407,"t":"loss","x":"1407: the north-west and west fall away.","cp":"page silent: the Khokhars of the Punjab, the chiefs of Mewat and local governors","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nasir-ud-Din_Mahmud_Shah_Tughluq","c":1},{"y":1414,"t":"dissolve","x":"1414: Khizr Khan takes Delhi and the Tughlaq dynasty is over.","m":6,"cp":"sayyid-dynasty","cpn":"Sayyid dynasty","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tughlaq_dynasty","c":3}],"wars":[{"name":"Siege of Warangal (Tughlaq)","from":1321,"to":1323,"outcome":"A first raid in 1321 failed; the siege of 1323 took Warangal, renamed Sultanpur, and annexed the kingdom.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muhammad_bin_Tughluq"},{"name":"Ghiyath al-Din's Bengal campaign","from":1324,"to":1325,"outcome":"Bengal brought under Delhi, invited by the Muslim aristocracy of Lakhnauti.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tughlaq_dynasty"},{"name":"Hammir Singh's recovery of Mewar","from":1326,"to":1336,"outcome":"Hammir Singh 'attempted to regain control of Mewar, but his initial efforts were thwarted' from 1326 (Mewar page); he 'liberated the strategic Rajputana following the victory in Battle of Singoli in 1336' (Muhammad bin Tughluq page) and Mewar left the…","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muhammad_bin_Tughluq"},{"name":"Conquest of Kampili","from":1327,"to":1327,"outcome":"Kampili destroyed; the enclave becomes Tughlaq land.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kampili_Kingdom"},{"name":"Revolts against Muhammad bin Tughluq","from":1327,"to":1351,"outcome":"'Revolts against Muhammad bin Tughlaq began in 1327'; Ma'bar 1334-35, Warangal 1336, Mewar 1336, Bengal by 1339, the Deccan 1347, Sind 1351.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tughlaq_dynasty"},{"name":"Firuz Shah's Bengal campaigns","from":1353,"to":1359,"outcome":"Invasion of Shamsuddin Ilyas Shah's Bengal in 1353: he withdrew to Ekdala and Firuz 'declined to annex'; a second march (the page dates it 1358, the Tughlaq page 'a war ... for 11 months in 1359') besieged Ekdala and ended in a peace with Sikandar Shah by…","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Firuz_Shah_Tughlaq"},{"name":"Firuz Shah's Odisha and Thatta expeditions","from":1360,"to":1363,"outcome":"Jajpur surrendered in 1360 with a tribute of 20 elephants a year; Thatta submitted in 1363 (after a failed march in 1362) with 400,000 tankas a year.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Firuz_Shah_Tughlaq"},{"name":"Nusrat Shah's rebellion","from":1394,"to":1397,"outcome":"Two sultans for three years, Mahmud at Delhi and Nusrat Shah at Firozabad; how it ended is not on the pages.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nasir-ud-Din_Mahmud_Shah_Tughluq"},{"name":"Timur's invasion of India","from":1398,"to":1399,"outcome":"Timur crossed the Indus on 30 September 1398, took Multan in October and sacked Delhi on 17-20 December ('the lowest point for the dynasty came in 1398'); he left without annexing Delhi and Multan passed to Khizr Khan under Timurid overlordship.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Delhi_(1398)"}],"certainty":[{"from":1320,"to":1414,"level":"soft","note":"No treaty or survey line is given by any page opened."}],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tughlaq_dynasty","title":"Tughlaq dynasty"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Delhi_(1398)","title":"Battle of Delhi (1398)"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Delhi_Sultanate","title":"Delhi Sultanate"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Firuz_Shah_Tughlaq","title":"Firuz Shah Tughlaq"},{"u